# Branch Naming Rule

New branches created from `develop` must follow the naming convention enforced by [.github/workflows/branch-name-check.yml](mdc:.github/workflows/branch-name-check.yml). Invalid names will fail the branch name check on pull requests.

## Format

Use a **prefix** followed by a **slug**:

```
<prefix>/<slug>
```

- **Prefix**: One of the allowed prefixes below.
- **Slug**: Lowercase letters and digits only, separated by `-` or `/`. No spaces or underscores.

## Allowed prefixes

| Prefix     | Use for |
|-----------|---------|
| `feature` | New features |
| `bugfix`  | Bug fixes |
| `hotfix`  | Urgent production fixes |
| `release` | Release preparation |
| `chore`   | Maintenance, tooling, config |
| `docs`    | Documentation only |
| `refactor`| Code refactoring (no new feature or bug fix) |
| `test`    | Adding or updating tests |

## Protected / special branches

These names are allowed as-is (no prefix/slug):

- `main`
- `master`
- `develop`

Bot branches (automated): `dependabot/*`, `renovate/*`.

## Valid pattern (regex)

Branch names must match:

```
^(main|master|develop|dependabot\/.+|renovate\/.+|(feature|bugfix|hotfix|release|chore|docs|refactor|test)\/[a-z0-9]+([-/][a-z0-9]+)*)$
```

## Examples

**Valid:**

- `feature/add-login`
- `feature/sku-price-history`
- `bugfix/fix-null-pointer`
- `hotfix/cart-checkout-race`
- `chore/update-deps`
- `docs/api-readme`
- `refactor/simplify-cart-store`
- `test/e2e-checkout`

**Invalid:**

- `Feature/add-login` — use lowercase prefix
- `feature/Add_Login` — slug must be lowercase, use `-` not `_`
- `add-login` — missing prefix (e.g. `feature/add-login`)
- `feat/add-login` — use `feature`, not `feat`

When creating or suggesting a new branch from `develop`, use this format so the branch passes the CI check on PR.
